{"page": 1, "kind": "text", "table": null, "row": null, "col": null, "x": null, "text": "*RCW 28A.230.095 requires districts to include a Civics CBA (OSPIDAS) at grade 4 or 5, 7 or 8, and 11 or 12 grade levels (indicated in blue).", "id": "u47"}
{"page": 1, "kind": "text", "table": null, "row": null, "col": null, "x": null, "text": "Civics CBAs are in bold above. While not required, OSPI recommends districts administer at least one additional Social Studies CBA in", "id": "u48"}
{"page": 1, "kind": "text", "table": null, "row": null, "col": null, "x": null, "text": "elementary, middle, and high school. The grade-level placements of OSPI Developed Assessments (CBAs) are recommendations and districts", "id": "u49"}
{"page": 1, "kind": "text", "table": null, "row": null, "col": null, "x": null, "text": "may choose to place CBAs at different grade levels within the same grade band. Districts may also create their own Social Studies CBAs. CBAs", "id": "u50"}
{"page": 1, "kind": "text", "table": null, "row": null, "col": null, "x": null, "text": "have not yet been aligned to the revised Social Studies Standards; this work is in progress.", "id": "u51"}
